# Prefix form, matching Stock's own vendor_property_contexts. The previous
# revision listed eight exact keys, which meant every other key the WMT stack
# writes fell through AOSP's `persist.vendor.` / `vendor.` catch-all to
# vendor_default_prop. The namespace belongs to the connectivity subsystem in
# its entirety; enumerating it bought nothing.
#
# Note the fall-through is a least-privilege problem, NOT a compile-time one:
# the neverallow on `vendor_default_prop:property_service set` is wrapped in
# compatible_property_only() (system/sepolicy/public/domain.te), and
# PRODUCT_COMPATIBLE_PROPERTY is false on this product because
# PRODUCT_SHIPPING_API_LEVEL is 26. An earlier revision of this comment said
# "a type no vendor domain may set", which is the same overstatement that was
# corrected in five other files this session -- vendor_init holds a blanket
# grant here, so the writes would have SUCCEEDED while being unlabelled and
# indistinguishable from every other vendor default. The prefix labels are
# still right; the reason is narrower than it claimed.
# persist.vendor.connsys.coredump.mode was deleted from vendor.prop (no reader).
persist.vendor.connsys.                   u:object_r:mtk_wmt_prop:s0
vendor.connsys.                           u:object_r:mtk_wmt_prop:s0
